.TH AVR\-VARIABLE\-SET 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-variable-set \- Create or replace a scoped value.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr variable set
[OPTIONS] [NAME]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create or replace a scoped value.
.PP
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-body\fR, \fB\-b\fR \fITEXT\fR
Variable value; otherwise prompt or read stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fITEXT\fR
Branch pattern; repeat for alternatives. (default: (); repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fITEXT\fR
Description for a newly created name; use edit to change an existing description.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR, \fB\-e\fR \fITEXT\fR
Environment pattern; repeat for alternatives. (default: (); repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-file\fR, \fB\-f\fR \fITEXT\fR
Read literal NAME=value entries from a dotenv file; no expansion.
.TP
\fB\-\-jq\fR, \fB\-q\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter JSON with an embedded jq expression.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output comma-separated fields, * for all, or ? to list fields.
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fITEXT\fR
Label for the scoped value.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug; does not broaden availability.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR, \fB\-R\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository full name or ID; defaults to the current checkout.
.TP
\fB\-\-repos\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization availability: repository names or IDs, comma-separated. (default: (); repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-variant\fR \fITEXT\fR
Select an existing scoped value by label.
.TP
\fB\-\-variant\-id\fR \fITEXT\fR
Select an existing scoped value by ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-visibility\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization availability: all, private, or selected (requires --repos).
.TP
\fB\-\-workflow\fR \fITEXT\fR
Workflow path pattern; repeat for alternatives. (default: (); repeatable)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-variable (1),
.BR avr-variable-delete (1),
.BR avr-variable-edit (1),
.BR avr-variable-get (1),
.BR avr-variable-list (1)
